tt-local-generator (0.46.3) noble; urgency=medium

  * fix(gallery): switching gallery density (comfortable <-> compact) now
    actually resizes ALREADY-RENDERED cards on both the native
    video/image/animate galleries and the artgen gallery, and freshly-built
    native cards honor the active density from construction instead of
    always being born comfortable-sized. Root cause: `ArtgenGallery.
    set_tile_size` and `MainWindow._apply_gallery_density` called
    `set_size_request()` on the OUTER card widget to "resize" an
    already-built card -- but `Gtk.Widget.set_size_request()` can only raise
    the minimum-size FLOOR, never shrink a widget below what its content
    already needs, so the pinned zone built at the OLD density (see
    `gallery_layout.pin_fixed_zone`, introduced in 0.46.0/328efe2) kept
    dominating the measured size and the switch was a visual no-op.
  * `gallery_layout.py` gains `thumb_size(density)` (thumbnail sub-zone size,
    scaled the same as `tile_size()`) and `set_pinned_size(zone, w, h)`,
    which resizes a `pin_fixed_zone()` zone's ANCHOR in place -- the anchor
    is a plain childless `Gtk.Box`, so its own measured min/natural size is
    always exactly its size_request, making this the one operation that
    actually changes what the zone reports on the next `measure()` pass.
    `pin_fixed_zone` now stashes its anchor on the returned zone
    (`zone._pin_anchor`) for `set_pinned_size` to find, and its docstring
    notes that it mutates the passed-in child's hexpand/vexpand/halign/
    valign properties.
  * `GenerationCard`/`PendingCard` (main_window.py) now resolve the live
    `gallery_density` setting at construction time and switched base class
    from `Gtk.Frame` to `Gtk.Box` -- Frame draws its own themed border from
    GTK's built-in fallback stylesheet even before any custom CSS loads,
    which sat as untracked chrome on top of whatever the pinned zone
    reported, so the card's own measured size could never land on an EXACT
    `gallery_layout.tile_size(density)` value. Each card's whole-content box
    is now wrapped in its own `pin_fixed_zone` (`self._card_zone`), and
    `_apply_gallery_density`/`ArtgenGallery.set_tile_size` resize each
    already-built card's `_card_zone` (and `_media_zone`/`_content_zone`
    thumbnail sub-zone) via `set_pinned_size` instead of only touching the
    outer widget's floor.
  * Test fix: `tests/conftest.py`'s `_isolate_app_settings` autouse fixture
    now also repatches `main_window._settings` to the fresh per-test
    `AppSettings` instance -- it was patching `app_settings.settings` and
    `create_param_panels._settings` but not `main_window`'s own
    already-bound reference, so any test driving `gallery_density` through
    `app_settings.settings` directly silently diverged from what
    `main_window.py`'s code actually read, causing order-dependent test
    flakiness once `GenerationCard`/`PendingCard` started reading it.

 -- Taylor Singletary <tsingletary@tenstorrent.com>  Fri, 17 Jul 2026 12:48:42 -0700

tt-local-generator (0.46.2) noble; urgency=medium

  * fix(gallery): media-entry cards are now a UNIFORM, FIXED size, identical
    across every Discover tab, instead of resizing to content and differing
    per gallery. Root causes: `GenerationCard` (main_window.py) set a fixed
    WIDTH but a NATURAL height (`set_size_request(_THUMB_W + 20, -1)`), and
    its thumbnail zone (`_make_scalable_thumb`) only set a size_request
    MINIMUM — a Gtk.Picture's own natural size follows the source image's
    intrinsic aspect ratio (a square 1024x1024 image naturally wants
    height == width, taller than a 16:9 floor), and Gtk.FlowBox
    (non-homogeneous) honors that larger natural request, so cards visibly
    grew/shrank per thumbnail content within a single gallery. Separately,
    the artgen gallery (`ArtgenGallery` in artgen_gallery.py) used a totally
    different tile size (110x90) and FlowBox grid settings
    (min_children_per_line=3) than the native video/image/animate galleries
    (~220 wide, min=2), so the SAME conceptual grid looked different on the
    artgen tab.
  * New `app/gallery_layout.py` — single source of truth for the card tile
    size (`TILE_W`/`TILE_H` = 220x240, empirically measured as the smallest
    height that acts as a true ceiling for every GenerationCard variant),
    the 16:9 thumbnail-zone size (`THUMB_W`/`THUMB_H`), the shared FlowBox
    grid settings, and `tile_size(density)` for the comfortable/compact
    density presets (now scaling BOTH dimensions uniformly — the density
    switch used to leave height at `-1`, silently re-introducing ragged
    cards at compact density). Also exposes `pin_fixed_zone(child, w, h)` —
    the one GTK trick (an invisible fixed-size anchor as a Gtk.Overlay's
    "main child", with the real content layered on top as a non-size-
    contributing overlay child) that pins a zone's MEASURED size regardless
    of its content's own aspect ratio/length.
  * `GenerationCard` now sets `self.set_size_request(TILE_W, TILE_H)` and
    wraps its whole media/thumbnail Gtk.Stack (`self._media_zone`) in
    `pin_fixed_zone`, so neither the static thumbnail, the hover-video, nor
    the GIF page can change the card's footprint. `PendingCard` matches the
    same fixed tile so a queued job's placeholder is never a different size
    than the finished card that replaces it.
  * `ArtgenGallery` cards use the SAME `gallery_layout` tile size and FlowBox
    settings, and pin their content zone the same way (content_fit switched
    COVER → CONTAIN to letterbox instead of crop, matching the native
    galleries). Fixed a hover-swap bug found while wiring this up: the GIF
    hover/leave handlers used to rip the whole content zone out of the card
    and replace it with an unpinned widget, so a hovered GIF card could
    still balloon to the animated widget's own aspect ratio — swaps now
    happen INSIDE the pinned zone (`remove_overlay`/`add_overlay`) so the
    tile size never changes across hover. New `ArtgenGallery.set_tile_size`
    keeps it in sync with `MainWindow._apply_gallery_density`.
  * Tests (TDD, `tests/test_gallery_card_uniform_size.py`, 9 new tests):
    GenerationCard and artgen-card fixed-size equality; card size
    independent of thumbnail content (square/16:9/missing); a genuine
    MEASURED-height regression check (not just the literal size_request)
    proving the media zone's natural size is capped, not merely floored;
    artgen card size independent of content aspect (image/text/empty);
    FlowBox grid settings identical across galleries; density scaling
    applied uniformly to the artgen gallery too; and the GIF hover-swap
    stability check. Full suite green (1668 passed, 1 skipped, 2
    known-flake deselected).

 -- Taylor Singletary <tsingletary@tenstorrent.com>  Fri, 17 Jul 2026 18:00:00 -0700

