    `_on_health_result` (port 8000), `_start_prompt_gen_health_worker`/
    `_prompt_gen_health_loop`/`_on_prompt_gen_health` (port 8001), and
    `_start_artgen_health_worker`/`_artgen_health_loop`/
    `_on_artgen_health_result` (port 8002) -- each of which ran its own
    background thread pinging a different port on its own timer and fed
    `_hw_statusbar` directly. `ModelStatusService` (SP-2) already reconciles
    all three signals into one polled, subscribable status map, so those
    threads were pure duplication of work the service was already doing.
    `_hw_statusbar` (the bottom-of-window aggregate server dot + per-
    capability dashboard popover) is now driven ENTIRELY by a single
    `self._status_service.subscribe(...)` callback
    (`_on_status_snapshot`/`_render_status_snapshot`), resolving the TODO(SP-3d)
    marker left at its construction site. Aggregation mirrors
    `ServersControl._refresh_bar_dot`'s policy (READY > STARTING > ERROR > OFF
    across every managed key); per-capability rows are grouped via
    `server_manager.servers_for_capability`. "Recover Jobs" (File menu) is now
    enabled purely from the service's video/image/animate READY state (no
    longer reads ControlPanel's `_server_launching`), and the Docker-log-tail
    auto-stop-on-ready behavior moved into the same snapshot handler. The
    one-shot AnimateDiff (Blackhole) hardware probe, previously nested inside
    `_start_artgen_health_worker` (which had no `ModelStatusService`
    equivalent, since "animatediff" has no `server_manager.SERVERS` entry), is
    preserved standalone as `_check_animatediff_hardware` -- and its
    3-tuple-vs-2-tuple `check_hardware()` unpacking bug (present since that
    return signature was added; every other caller in the codebase already
    unpacked 3 values) is fixed along the way, so the "animatediff" capability
    row can finally report real hardware state instead of always reading
    "unavailable". `do_close_request` no longer tears down three separate
    stop-events/threads -- just `self._status_unsubscribe()` alongside
    `self._status_service.stop()`. ControlPanel/ArtgenPanel are untouched
    (deletion is SP-3d-5, next); this task's whole point was retiring the
    `_controls.set_server_state`/`_controls._server_launching` reads inside
    the now-deleted health-result handlers so that deletion has nothing left
    to trip over. New tests: tests/test_main_window_status_service_snapshot.py.

