tt-local-generator (0.43.1) noble; urgency=medium

  * SP-3d-3 review fix: `_running_generation_server()` was capability-BLIND --
    it checked `ready_keys("video")` then `ready_keys("image")` unconditionally
    regardless of what the caller actually cared about. Since every
    video/image/animate/skyreels `ServerDef` shares ONE port (8000) and is
    mutually exclusive with the others, this meant a caller asking "is video
    ready" would wrongly see "ready" whenever an UNRELATED capability's model
    (e.g. FLUX, "image") happened to be loaded instead -- a real regression
    versus ControlPanel's old `_server_ready`, which was mismatch-aware (see
    `ControlPanel.set_server_state`'s `mismatch = source_for_model !=
    current_source` check). Two reachable bugs: TT-TV's `get_server_status`
    would report "ready" and auto-generate video prompts against a FLUX
    server (failing every attempt while showing "ready"), and `_on_generate`'s
    AnimateDiff-blackhole chip-busy guard could misfire off an unrelated
    capability's loaded model. Fixed: `_running_generation_server(capability)`
    now takes an explicit capability and checks ONLY that one. Threaded
    through both call sites -- a new `_attractor_capability()` derives the
    capability from the current medium (mirroring the AnimateDiff/artgen
    special-cases `_on_health_result` already used), and the AnimateDiff-
    blackhole guard now passes `"video"` explicitly (it's a video-capability
    model, and that branch only ever runs for `model_source == "video"`).
    `_on_open_attractor`'s inline `get_server_status` lambda was also
    extracted into a real method, `_attractor_server_status`, so this
    capability-scoping is independently testable without constructing a real
    `attractor.AttractorWindow`. New regression tests confirmed failing
    against the pre-fix code (capability-blind) and passing post-fix.

