tt-local-generator (0.29.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Field roles in the pipeline editor -- the Create surface's field vocabulary
    now applies to Pipeline Studio's Remix/Compose editor, so a field means the
    same thing everywhere.
    - Every editable node field carries the same marker as Create: a pencil
      (your words -- text the model renders), a spark (the model chooses from
      this value), or a gear (exact setting the model never reads).
    - A step card's fields are ordered brief -> direction -> control, and the
      deterministic (gear) fields are tucked under a per-card collapsed
      "Controls (N)" disclosure, so the creative inputs lead.
    - Brief (creative-words) text fields gain a contextual modifier-pill "Add"
      affordance: the chip bank is chosen by the node's output kind (an
      image-output node offers image chips, video offers video, gif offers
      animate; text/LLM nodes get none). Applied pill text is folded into that
      field's value at Run time ("<original text> <pill text>").
    - Edit-contract preserved: a field with no retyping and no applied pill
      still collects to its unchanged original value, so an untouched remix
      run reproduces the base run exactly (empty edit diff).
    - Built on the shared, GTK-free `field_roles` layer (deepened
      `classify_pipeline_field`, new `marker_prefix` formatter) and the
      `ModifierPills` widget, both introduced with the Create surface -- no
      duplication, and generation / derive_spec are untouched.

