tt-local-generator (0.28.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Create surface redesign -- every field now says what it does, models scale,
    and width overflow is impossible by construction. Fixes four reported
    problems on the Create surface.
    - Role zones: each medium's fields are grouped into "Your brief" (the
      creative input the model renders), "Direction" (things that steer the
      result), and a collapsed "Controls" (deterministic knobs). Every field
      carries a marker -- a pencil (your words), a spark (the model chooses
      from this value), or a gear (exact setting the model never reads) -- so
      you can tell LLM-interpreted choices from raw input at a glance.
    - The modifier "fun" is back as removable pills: tap a Camera/Lighting/
      Mood/Style chip in the Direction zone to add a pill (an applied chip
      hides until you remove its pill), and the applied modifier text is
      appended to the brief at generate time.
    - Models: the persistent flat "live-model strip" that overflowed the
      window is retired. Picking a model within a medium is now a dropdown
      scoped to that medium's own models; browsing the whole collection is the
      "Start with a model" door -- a wrapping grid grouped Image / Video /
      Animate / Text (classified by each server's capabilities), which scales
      to any number of models without overflowing.
    - The whole surface is width-clamped (gtk_layout.wrap_centered) and every
      multi-item row wraps, so it can never exceed the window again.
    - New shared, GTK-free `field_roles` layer (role + marker taxonomy and
      classifiers) so the same vocabulary can drive pipeline field
      configuration in a later change. `MaxWidthBin`/`wrap_centered` extracted
      to a shared `gtk_layout` module.
    - Migration-safe: generation is untouched -- each panel's collect() output
      dict is byte-for-byte compatible, and the model value the scoped dropdown
      produces matches what the old panel field produced. The legacy per-model
      tabs remain the reachable fallback.

