tt-local-generator (0.9.2) noble; urgency=medium

  * artgen: auto-discover externally-started chat servers. Endpoint detection
    now sweeps local ports for any OpenAI-compatible chat model instead of only
    probing the app's own artgen (8002) and prompt-gen (8001) ports. A model
    launched outside the app on a non-standard port (e.g. a vLLM Llama-3.3-70B
    on 8003) is now found and used, and the tiny prompt-gen fallback is ranked
    last so a real chat model always wins over it.
  * mcp_server: route _make_call_fn through the same discovery for consistency.
  * TTLG_ARTGEN_SCAN_PORTS env var overrides the swept port list.
  * mcp_server: move default port 8003 -> 8120 (still TTLG_MCP_PORT-overridable)
    so it no longer collides with a chat model started on 8003 and stays outside
    the artgen port sweep. tt-ctl mcp-config and plugin docs updated to match.
  * UI: the Servers popover (non-autohide, so it stays open while a service
    boots) now dismisses when the main window loses focus, instead of lingering
    on top of other applications' windows after an app switch.
  * artgen: the panel's health indicator now uses the same endpoint discovery
    as the generation router, so a model started on a non-standard port shows
    as "on" (and its name is displayed) instead of falsely reading offline.
    The 5s poll re-pings the cached endpoint and only re-sweeps when it drops.
  * UI: the Servers popover reconciles its artgen rows against discovery, so the
    row for the actually-loaded model lights up wherever it is served (and only
    that row, fixing the prior quirk where all artgen rows lit whenever 8002 was
    up).
  * tests: fix stale test_worker_animatediff mocks (check_hardware now returns
    a 3-tuple (ok, msg, num_chips) after the multi-chip change).

