tt-local-generator (0.3.3) noble; urgency=medium

  * prompt engine: six structural slug templates rotate the syntactic shape
    of every algorithmically-generated video/SkyReels prompt so the LLM
    receives different sentence patterns on each call.
  * prompt engine: UNEXPECTED_JUXTAPOSITIONS word bank (24 entries) injected
    at 12 % probability as a sixth slot — surreal modifiers the LLM cannot
    remove without violating its "keep every element" instruction.
  * prompt engine: adaptive LLM sampling — temperature, top_p, and max_tokens
    scale to model size (0.6 B → temp 1.05; 7-8 B → 0.85; 13-14 B → 0.75;
    30 B+ → 0.65); small models (<3 B) run n=3 candidates and the one with
    the highest content-word specificity score is selected.
  * prompt engine: anti-repetition sliding window (last 20 slugs); slugs with
    Jaccard similarity ≥ 0.35 against any recent slug are retried up to 5 times
    before accepting the least-similar candidate.
  * prompt engine: Markov state_size lowered 2 → 1 on the 498-line corpus,
    producing genuinely wild sentence-level recombinations instead of near-
    verbatim replay.
  * artgen: circuit generator now defaults --circuit-style to random, cycling
    through all diagram styles on each generation.
  * artgen/ansi: _normalize_grid no longer strips trailing blank rows that fall
    within the target canvas height — BBS void zones (rows 1-2, 18-20) are
    intentional and must be preserved.
  * settings: animatediff_frames preference added (default 8); Preferences
    dialog exposes it with a SpinButton; replaces the hardcoded frames=8.
  * tests: AnimateDiffGenerationWorker covered (hardware failure, subprocess
    failure, happy path, cancellation); test_prompt_client updated to use
    urllib.request mocking throughout.

 -- Taylor Singletary <tsingletary@tenstorrent.com>  Fri, 23 May 2026 10:00:00 -0700

tt-local-generator (0.3.2) noble; urgency=medium

  * artgen: ANSI generation rewritten as a 3-pass pipeline — ASCII structure
    (spatial composition, plain chars, 1024 tokens) → block refinement (Unicode
    block chars ░▒▓█▀▄▌▐, 1024 tokens) → colorization (xterm-256 foreground
    \033[38;5;Nm█ per cell, 8192 tokens). Separating composition from character
    selection from color assignment gives coherent imagery instead of palette strips.
  * artgen: switch ANSI format from background+space (\033[48;5;Nm ) to
    foreground+block (\033[38;5;Nm█) — brighter, more vibrant output in all terminals.
  * artgen: ArtGenerator base class gains generate_artifact(args, call_fn) hook for
    multi-pass pipelines; AnsiGenerator overrides it; all other generators use the
    single-pass default. First prototype of the remix-mode multi-pass pattern.
  * artgen cli: _make_call_fn() closure supports per-call max_tokens override so each
    pipeline pass can tune its own token budget independently.
  * artgen panel: updated to call generate_artifact() instead of inline pipeline;
    accumulates usage across all passes in a single MediaRecord.
  * docs: README and website explain the 3-pass ANSI pipeline; CLAUDE.md documents
    the generate_artifact hook and multi-pass architecture.

